# Key names for local secrets. ASP.NET Core does not load a .env file.
# Prefer `dotnet user-secrets` on Product.ApplicationRoot (already has UserSecretsId).
# Nested keys use `__` in environment variables and `:` in user-secrets / appsettings.
# Do not commit secrets.
#
# From Solution/product/src/Product.ApplicationRoot:
#   dotnet user-secrets set "WebApi:ClientId" "..."
#   dotnet user-secrets set "WebApi:ClientSecret" "..."
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Bff:ClientId" "..."
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Bff:ClientSecret" "..."
#   dotnet user-secrets set "Portal:AllowList:0" "idp-subject-or-email"
#   dotnet user-secrets set "ConnectionStrings:ProductStore" "Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=product_service;Username=jdples"
#   dotnet user-secrets set "ApplicationInsights:ConnectionString" "..."
#
# Equivalent process environment variables (override user secrets if both are set):

# Identity__Authority=https://dev.auth.alpha.org

# Product.WebApi client credentials (scope alpha.idp.read)
# WebApi__ClientId=
# WebApi__ClientSecret=

# Product.Bff interactive OIDC (scope alpha.idp.readwrite)
# Bff__ClientId=
# Bff__ClientSecret=
# Bff__CountryCode=za
# Demo client redirect URIs: https://localhost:5173/signin-oidc and https://localhost:7127/signin-oidc
# (plus matching signout-callback-oidc post-logout URIs).
# CountryCode: production `global` (IDP default). IDP dev cannot use that identifier; local fallback is `za`.

# Portal allow-list (IDP subject or email, comma-separated)
# Portal__AllowList=

# ConnectionStrings__ProductStore=Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=product_service;Username=username

# ApplicationInsights__ConnectionString=
